    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                    The Hogarth Press replies to prior letters sent by Gordon A. Baxter. They grant permission for the use of an extract from The Common Reader, offering a reduced fee of one and a half guineas. At the back of this first reply, there is also a reply, dated 30 April 1940, where they finally agree to the use of a reduced passage for a fee of one guinea.
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1940-04-18">
                            18th April, 1940.
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <persName key="MAPP0082">G.A. Baxter, <choice><abbr>Esq.</abbr><expan>Esquire</expan></choice></persName>,
                        </addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Abbey Street,</addrLine>
                        <addrLine><placeName>Melrose,</placeName></addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Roxburgshire.</addrLine>
                    </address>
                    <salute>
                        Dear Sir,
                    </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Woolf – <title>
                        <choice><orig>Common Reader</orig>
                            <reg>The Common Reader</reg></choice>, First Series
                            </title>
                        <note><p>The Common Reader is a collection of essays by Virginia Woolf, exploring the value of reading for pleasure for the common readers. The first of the two series was published in 1925.</p></note>
                </p>
                <p>
                    In reply to your letter of April 9th, we shall be glad to give you <lb/>
                    permission to use the passage you quote, i.e. from &quot;Admitting the vagueness&quot; <lb/>
                    down to &quot;than custom would have us believe it,&quot; from the above book, on pay-<lb/>
                    ment of a fee of one and a half guiness. Our minimum fee for extracts from <lb/>
                    Mrs. Woolf<note><p>The author refers here to <persName key="Q40909">Virginia Woolf</persName>.</p></note>'s works is usually a guinea a page so we hope that the reduced fee <lb/>
                    will be satisfactory to you. We take it the usual acknowledgements will be <lb/>
                    made.
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>
                        Yours faithfully,
                    </salute>
                    <signed>
                        THE HOGARTH PRESS
                    </signed>
                    <seg type="position">
                        Manager.
                    </seg>
                </closer>
            </div>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1940-04-30">
                            30th April, 1940.
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <persName>G.A. Baxter, <choice><abbr>Esq.</abbr><expan>Esquire</expan></choice></persName>,
                        </addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Abbey Street,</addrLine>
                        <addrLine><placeName>Melrose,</placeName></addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Roxburgshire.</addrLine>
                    </address>
                    <salute>
                        Dear Sir,
                    </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>Woolf – <title>The Common Reader, 1st  Series</title></p>
                <p>
                    Thank you for your letter of April 24th. We shall be glad <lb/>
                    to give you permission to use the reduced passage from the above book <lb/>
                    for a fee of one guinea.
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>
                        Yours faithfully,
                    </salute>
                    <signed>
                        THE HOGARTH PRESS
                    </signed>
                    <seg type="position">
                        Manager.
                    </seg>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
